 826               
 827               /       CALL WITH:
 828               
 829               /       TAD     CHAR                    /AC CONTAINS LATEST CHARACTER TO OUTPUT
 830               /       JMS I   (PFFOUT)                /CALL ROUTINE
 831               /       JMP     FILEFULL                /THE FILE BECAME FULL AND WAS CLOSED OUT
 832               /       JMP     FILEOK                  /FILE IS STILL ACTIVE
 833               
 834               /       FILES WILL BE CLOSED OUT IF:
 835               
 836               /       A)      A NON-<EOL> IS PASSED AND THERE IS ONLY ROOM ENOUGH FOR THE
 837               /               NON-<EOL> CHARACTER AND AN ADDITIONAL <EOL> CHARACTER AND <EOF>.
 838               /               AN <EOL> WILL BE AUTOMATICALLY INSERTED TO PRESERVE THE INTEGRITY
 839               /               OF THE FILE ALONG WITH AN <EOF> TO CLOSE IT. THE FILE WILL ALSO
 840               /               BE WRITTEN OUT TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE ACCORDING TO THE PRIOR
 841               /               INITIALIZATION (SEE "PFFINIT").
 842               
 843               /       B)      AN <EOL> CHARACTER (0000) IS PASSED AND THERE IS LESS ROOM THAN
 844               /               "EOLPROT" LEFT IN THE FILE. AN <EOF> WILL BE INSERTED INTO THE FILE
 845               /               AND IT WILL BE CLOSED AND WRITTEN OUT TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE ACCORDING
 846               /               TO THE PRIOR INITIALIZATION (SEE "PFFINIT").
 847               
 848               /       C)      AN <EOF> CHARACTER (4000) IS PASSED. IF THE PREVIOUS CHARACTER WAS
 849               /               NOT AN <EOL> CHARACTER, ONE WILL BE INSERTED BEFORE AN <EOF> IS
 850               /               INSERTED. THE FILE WILL BE CLOSED AND WRITTEN OUT TO THE SYSTEM
 851               /               DEVICE ACCORDING TO THE PRIOR INITIALIZATION (SEE "PFFINIT").
 852               
